      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n\n \nUsers who have both pending and claimable deposits can become permanently invisible to the Investment Manager after claiming their fulfilled shares, causing their still-pending deposits to be ignored and potentially stuck forever. \n \nIn the ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol: \n \n```solidity \n\nfunction mint(uint256 shares, address receiver, address controller) public nonReentrant returns (uint256 assets) { \n    // ... authorization and checks ... \n \n    uint256 availableShares = $.claimableDepositShares[controller]; \n    uint256 availableAssets = $.claimableDepositAssets[controller]; \n \n    // ... proportional calculation ... \n \n    // ← BUG IS HERE: \n    if (availableShares == shares) { \n @>       $.activeDepositRequesters.remove(controller);   // ← WRONG: removes too early! \n        delete $.claimableDepositShares[controller]; \n        delete $.claimableDepositAssets[controller]; \n    } else { \n        $.claimableDepositShares[controller] -= shares; \n        $.claimableDepositAssets[controller] -= assets; \n    } \n \n    // ... emit + transfer ... \n} \n``` \nSame issue exists in the deposit(uint256 assets, ...) function. \n\n \n```solidity \nfunction deposit(uint256 assets, address receiver, address controller) public nonReentrant returns (uint256 shares) { \n\n    VaultStorage storage $ = _getVaultStorage(); \n\n    if (!(controller == msg.sender || IERC7540($.shareToken).isOperator(controller, msg.sender))) { \n\n        revert InvalidCaller(); \n\n    } \n\n    if (assets == 0) revert ZeroAssets(); \n\n    uint256 availableShares = $.claimableDepositShares[controller]; \n\n    uint256 availableAssets = $.claimableDepositAssets[controller]; \n\n    if (assets > availableAssets) revert InsufficientClaimableAssets(); \n\n    // Calculate shares proportionally from the stored asset-share ratio \n\n    shares = assets.mulDiv(availableShares, availableAssets, Math.Rounding.Floor); \n\n    if (shares == 0) revert ZeroSharesCalculated(); \n\n    // Remove from active deposit requesters if no more claimable assets \n\n  @>  if (availableAssets == assets) {   // ← BUG STARTS HERE \n\n  @>      $.activeDepositRequesters.remove(controller);// Bug here \n\n        delete $.claimableDepositShares[controller]; \n\n        delete $.claimableDepositAssets[controller]; \n\n    } else { \n\n        $.claimableDepositShares[controller] -= shares; \n\n        $.claimableDepositAssets[controller] -= assets; \n\n    } \n\n    emit Deposit(receiver, controller, assets, shares); \n\n    // Transfer shares from vault to receiver using ShareToken \n\n    if (!IERC20Metadata($.shareToken).transfer(receiver, shares)) { \n\n        revert ShareTransferFailed(); \n\n    } \n\n} \n``` \n\nThe vault removes a user from the activeDepositRequesters set as soon as they fully claim their claimable shares, without checking whether they still have pending deposits waiting to be fulfilled. If a user has both claimable and pending deposits, claiming the claimable portion makes them disappear from the active list → the investment manager may skip fulfilling their remaining pending assets → funds get stuck forever. \n \n\nExploit Scenario: \n\nAlice calls requestDeposit(100). (Status: Pending: 100, ActiveSet: Yes) \n\nManager calls fulfillDeposit(Alice). (Status: Pending: 0, Claimable: 100, ActiveSet: Yes) \n\nAlice calls requestDeposit(50). (Status: Pending: 50, Claimable: 100, ActiveSet: Yes) \n\nAlice calls deposit(100) to claim her shares. \n\nResult: The contract sees availableAssets == assets (100 == 100) and removes Alice from activeDepositRequesters. \n\nConsequence: Alice still has 50 pending assets, but she is no longer in the activeDepositRequesters list. The Investment Manager will not see her in the active set when looking for requests to fulfill. \n\n \n\nImpact  \n\nUsers with both pending and claimable deposits risk having their pending requests ignored or stuck indefinitely because claiming the claimable part removes them from the active tracking set used by the Investment Manager for fulfillment \n \n\n\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nOnly remove from activeDepositRequesters if both claimable and pending deposits are zero, by adding a check for pendingDepositAssets[controller] == 0 before removal. \n\nOR \nsimply \nOnly remove the controller if they have no pending assets remaining. \n\n```Solidity \n\nif (availableAssets == assets) { \n    // Check if there are no pending assets before removing \n    if ($.pendingDepositAssets[controller] == 0) { \n        $.activeDepositRequesters.remove(controller); \n    } \n    delete $.claimableDepositShares[controller]; \n    delete $.claimableDepositAssets[controller]; \n} \n``` \n\nPlease also apply the same fix to withdraw()",
      "proofOfConcept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport \"../src/ERC20Faucet.sol\";\nimport \"../src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol\";\nimport \"../src/ShareTokenUpgradeable.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\n\ncontract ActiveDepositRequestersBugTest is Test {\n    ERC7575VaultUpgradeable public vault;\n    ShareTokenUpgradeable public shareToken;\n    ERC20Faucet public asset;\n\n    address public alice = address(0x1);\n    address public investmentManager = address(0x2);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        // Deploy and initialize ShareToken\n        ShareTokenUpgradeable shareTokenImpl = new ShareTokenUpgradeable();\n        bytes memory shareTokenData = abi.encodeWithSelector(\n            ShareTokenUpgradeable.initialize.selector,\n            \"Test Share Token\",\n            \"tSHARE\",\n            address(this)\n        );\n        ERC1967Proxy shareTokenProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(address(shareTokenImpl), shareTokenData);\n        shareToken = ShareTokenUpgradeable(address(shareTokenProxy));\n\n        // Deploy asset with sufficient supply\n        asset = new ERC20Faucet(\"TestAsset\", \"ASSET\", 100000000e18);\n\n        // Deploy and initialize Vault\n        ERC7575VaultUpgradeable vaultImpl = new ERC7575VaultUpgradeable();\n        bytes memory vaultData = abi.encodeWithSelector(\n            ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.initialize.selector,\n            asset,\n            address(shareToken),\n            address(this)\n        );\n        ERC1967Proxy vaultProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(address(vaultImpl), vaultData);\n        vault = ERC7575VaultUpgradeable(address(vaultProxy));\n\n        // Register vault with share token\n        shareToken.registerVault(address(asset), address(vault));\n\n        // Set investment manager\n        vault.setInvestmentManager(investmentManager);\n\n        // Fund alice with sufficient assets (minimum deposit is 1000e18)\n        // We need at least 3500e18 for both deposits (1500e18 + 2000e18)\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 2 hours);\n        asset.faucetAmountFor(alice, 100000e18);\n\n        // Approve vault to spend alice's assets\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        asset.approve(address(vault), type(uint256).max);\n    }\n\n   \n    function testActiveDepositRequestersRemovalBug() public {\n        uint256 firstDepositAmount = 1500e18;\n        uint256 secondDepositAmount = 2000e18;\n\n        // ===== STEP 1: Alice requests first deposit =====\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        vault.requestDeposit(firstDepositAmount, alice, alice);\n\n        // Verify: Alice should be in activeDepositRequesters\n        address[] memory activeRequesters1 = vault.getActiveDepositRequesters();\n        assertEq(activeRequesters1.length, 1, \"Step 1: One active requester expected\");\n        assertEq(activeRequesters1[0], alice, \"Step 1: Alice should be in active requesters\");\n\n        // Verify: Alice has pending deposit\n        uint256 pendingBefore = vault.pendingDepositRequest(0, alice);\n        assertEq(pendingBefore, firstDepositAmount, \"Step 1: Alice should have 1500e18 pending\");\n\n        // ===== STEP 2: Investment Manager fulfills first deposit =====\n        vm.prank(investmentManager);\n        vault.fulfillDeposit(alice, firstDepositAmount);\n\n        // Verify: Alice still in activeDepositRequesters\n        address[] memory activeRequesters2 = vault.getActiveDepositRequesters();\n        assertEq(activeRequesters2.length, 1, \"Step 2: Alice still in active set after fulfill\");\n\n        // Verify: First deposit is now claimable\n        uint256 claimableBefore = vault.claimableDepositRequest(0, alice);\n        assertEq(claimableBefore, firstDepositAmount, \"Step 2: 1500e18 should be claimable\");\n\n        // ===== STEP 3: Alice requests SECOND deposit while still having claimable =====\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        vault.requestDeposit(secondDepositAmount, alice, alice);\n\n        // Verify: Alice's state before claiming\n        uint256 pendingAfterSecondRequest = vault.pendingDepositRequest(0, alice);\n        uint256 claimableAfterSecondRequest = vault.claimableDepositRequest(0, alice);\n        assertEq(pendingAfterSecondRequest, secondDepositAmount, \"Step 3: Should have 2000e18 pending\");\n        assertEq(claimableAfterSecondRequest, firstDepositAmount, \"Step 3: Should still have 1500e18 claimable\");\n\n        // Verify: Alice in activeDepositRequesters with both pending and claimable\n        address[] memory activeRequesters3 = vault.getActiveDepositRequesters();\n        assertEq(activeRequesters3.length, 1, \"Step 3: Alice still in active set (has both pending and claimable)\");\n        assertEq(activeRequesters3[0], alice, \"Step 3: Alice should be active\");\n\n        // ===== STEP 4: Alice claims her claimable deposit (THE BUG TRIGGERS HERE) =====\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        vault.deposit(firstDepositAmount, alice, alice);\n\n        // ===== STEP 5: CHECK THE IMPACT - ALICE IS NOW INVISIBLE =====\n        address[] memory activeRequestersAfterClaim = vault.getActiveDepositRequesters();\n\n        // BUG REVEALED: Alice is removed from activeDepositRequesters entirely\n        assertEq(\n            activeRequestersAfterClaim.length,\n            0,\n            \"BUG CONFIRMED: Alice removed from active set even though she has 2000e18 pending!\"\n        );\n\n        // CRITICAL: Verify Alice STILL HAS pending deposit that now cannot be found by Investment Manager\n        uint256 pendingAfterClaim = vault.pendingDepositRequest(0, alice);\n        assertEq(\n            pendingAfterClaim,\n            secondDepositAmount,\n            \"BUG CONFIRMED: Alice's 2000e18 pending deposit is still there but invisible!\"\n        );\n\n        // IMPACT PROOF: Verify the vulnerability is real\n        assertTrue(\n            pendingAfterClaim > 0 && activeRequestersAfterClaim.length == 0,\n            \"VULNERABILITY PROVEN: Pending deposit exists but requester is invisible to Investment Manager\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n```",
